; CancellationLowering turns Julia master's cancellation points (`julia.cancellation_point()`
; calls) into reset regions: a stack buffer that is filled by setjmp and published in the
; task, and closed again before anything a jump back to it could tear, and before
; returning. The runtime facts are given explicitly (x86_64 Linux's), so that the output
; doesn't depend on the host.

